<section id="tradeoffs" class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="section-y mx-auto flex max-w-page flex-col gap-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="flex max-w-[40rem] flex-col items-start gap-5">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-accent uppercase">Tradeoffs</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-balance md:text-5xl">Telos is not the cheapest way to use Claude Code.</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        In our benchmark, Telos cost more than bare Claude Code or a static <code class="font-mono text-text">CLAUDE.md</code>
        on every task we measured, with about the same acceptance rate.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-md border border-line bg-surface p-6 md:p-8">
        <h3 class="m-0 text-xl font-semibold md:text-2xl">Choose Telos</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text">When you want phases, recorded decisions and acceptance checks on a project that spans many sessions.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">We did not measure that long-term value.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-md border border-line bg-surface p-6 md:p-8">
        <h3 class="m-0 text-xl font-semibold md:text-2xl">Skip it</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text">For small one-off tasks, or when token cost is your main concern.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Measured by the Telos author on two repositories, 120 runs.</p>
  </div>
</section>
